{#
  Coding Assignment 3 - Feature A: Welcome new members
  Design Claim 18 (Chapter 5): friendly interactions with existing members soon after joining
  help newcomers stay longer and contribute more.
  Design Claim 20 (Chapter 5): welcomers help newcomers. Here every existing member can be a welcomer.
#}
<div class="col-md-8 mx-auto mb-4">
  <div class="card shadow-sm">
    <div class="card-body">
      <h5 class="card-title mb-1">🌱 Say hello to our new members</h5>
      <p class="text-muted small mb-3">They joined in the last {{ newcomer_days }} days. A friendly first reply makes newcomers much more likely to stay!</p>

      {% for post in newcomers_to_welcome %}
      <div class="border rounded p-2 mb-2">
        <div class="d-flex justify-content-between">
          <a href="/u/{{ post.username }}"><strong>@{{ post.username }}</strong></a>
          <span class="badge bg-success">New member 🌱</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-2">{{ post.content|truncate(120) }}</p>

        <!-- The welcome message is ready but can be changed. It is sent as a normal comment
             (so it also goes through the friendly check from Coding Assignment 2). -->
        <form action="{{ url_for('add_comment', post_id=post.id) }}" method="POST" class="d-flex gap-2">
          <input type="text" class="form-control form-control-sm" name="content" required
                 value="Welcome to MiniSocial, @{{ post.username }}! 👋 Happy to have you here.">
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-success btn-sm text-nowrap">Say welcome 👋</button>
        </form>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>